('Hotel','41',41,'Private Transfer',NULL,NULL,NULL,'09:00 – Leaving from Baku to Gobustan (1 way x 45 mins)  10:00 – Arrive at Gobustan National Park  - Visit Gobustan National Park, a UNESCO World Heritage site known for its ancient petroglyphs, rock formations, and archaeological heritage dating back more than 40,000 years. The open-air museum offers insights into prehistoric human life, hunting traditions, and early settlements. After exploring the site, continue to the nearby Mud Volcanoes—one of the largest mud volcano fields in the world. The unique grey, lunar-like landscape and constantly bubbling mud pools create an unforgettable natural experience and an excellent spot for photos.  12:00 – Leaving Gobustan to Baku  13:00 – Lunch Break  14:00 –Evening City Tour starts with panoramic full evening city view of Baku followed by:  - Highland Park (Which is the highest point in the Azerbaijani capital, opening a panoramic view of the city and its bay. The city''s residents and visitors often come here to see a bird''s eye view of Baku, and just have a walk. The Upland Park can be reached by cable railway (funicular) in 7-8 minutes from the boulevard or by climbing up the endless stone stairs.)  - Flame Towers (The city''s tallest building. The height of 182 m. Flame Towers - consisting of three high-rise buildings in the complex.)   18:00 – Dinner Break (if includes)  19:00 – Drop to the Hotel    Overnight in Baku',NULL,NULL,'Sedan - 4 Seaters (Local Speaking)',41.0),
